00:03:56.706 --> 00:03:59.987
The goal of our podcast is to communicate and celebrate science,

00:04:00.388 --> 00:04:05.530
but science is incomplete when black scientists and other scientists of color are oppressed,

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:12.893
and our understanding of science is incomplete if we ignore the historical and present-day influence of racism.

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:18.435
The discussion going on around our country right now was sparked by things that have happened

00:04:18.906 --> 00:04:22.428
on the streets regarding law enforcement, regarding the judicial system,

00:04:22.988 --> 00:04:29.051
but these issues go into every aspect of our society, which includes science and education,

00:04:29.431 --> 00:04:32.072
the kinds of things that we ourselves are involved in.

00:04:32.492 --> 00:04:34.953
Now is the time to listen and learn.

00:04:35.293 --> 00:04:40.495
Along with this statement on our social media and in the description of this episode of the podcast,

00:04:40.965 --> 00:04:45.407
we've shared links that include many resources for understanding racial injustice

00:04:45.767 --> 00:04:49.869
and the ways we can all help, including within the fields of science and education.

00:04:50.249 --> 00:04:56.032
We have been, we the two of us, have been and still are exploring these references,

00:04:56.652 --> 00:04:59.433
educating ourselves, and we invite you to join us.

00:05:00.005 --> 00:05:08.369
