00:46:35.267 --> 00:46:49.912
So it is thought that this deposit was up to 400 kilometers offshore of what at this time was the landmass of Laurentia, which today makes up part of North America, and at that time was near the equator.

00:46:49.927 --> 00:47:00.811
Eventually this continental chunk moved and then was thrust upward during the rising of the Canadian Rockies, so now they are up in the air and exposed.

00:47:01.071 --> 00:47:06.992
But yeah, this was an out-in-the-ocean deposit. Relatively deep waters, too.

00:47:07.332 --> 00:47:11.053
Yeah, which is not what we usually get from ocean material.

00:47:11.125 --> 00:47:15.846
