00:47:48.731 --> 00:47:49.551
Good name.

00:47:49.765 --> 00:48:01.349
So next to this site was a cliff thought to have been about 200 meters high, and on the top of that cliff would have been a tropical platform.

00:48:01.609 --> 00:48:14.112
Carbonate rocks, you know, reef-type things, you go down the drop-off, Finding Nemo style, at the bottom of that cliff is this fossil ecosystem.

00:48:14.508 --> 00:48:23.850
Although, the fact that there's algae, photosynthetic algae in the Burgess Shale, suggests that it wasn't totally dark, that there would have been some sunlight reaching down there.

00:48:24.271 --> 00:48:36.934
It's thought that the deposits at the Burgess Shale are created in large part by mudflows, so occasional landslides of mud basically, down parts of the cliff that would create these rapid deposits.

00:48:36.989 --> 00:48:41.871
