The things that are famously known to fossilize well.

00:53:33.166 --> 00:53:37.767
Which is a beautiful demonstration of the bias in the fossil record.

00:53:38.007 --> 00:53:38.247
Yep.

00:53:38.628 --> 00:53:53.292
The fact that the fossil record does much better at hard mineralized things. The Burgess Shale isn't a glimpse into what an actual Cambrian ecosystem might have looked like.

00:53:53.312 --> 00:53:53.552
Yes.

00:53:54.086 --> 00:54:02.950
Because the ratio of soft things to hard things in this ecosystem is much more similar to modern day ecosystems.

00:54:03.070 --> 00:54:18.856
This is a good comparison to make here. If you were to take a section of your backyard and flash turn it into a fossil site, age it 12 million years, and now you suddenly have a fossil site you can look at.

