00:57:42.386 --> 00:57:49.889
Yeah. It might be that the clay had a bit of an antibacterial aspect just because the minerals in the clay weren't a good place for bacteria to be.

00:57:50.029 --> 00:58:00.773
Oh yeah. And like we see this in certain clays and sediments today where there are, you know, vitamin properties and animals will eat them to counteract ailments and stuff.

00:58:00.993 --> 00:58:01.253
Right.

00:58:01.613 --> 00:58:02.513
Very interesting.

00:58:03.002 --> 00:58:11.306
Overall, it's probably, as so many things are, a combination of factors because if it wasn't, we'd probably have a better idea of what exactly happened.

